  "copy": {
    "fr": {
      "tagline": "Un casse-briques ou l'on ne rattrape pas directement la bille. Vise bien pour faire un maximum de rebond en un seul tir. Touche ensuite l'écran pour activer les interrupteur afin de piéger la bille entre les briques.",
      "tags": [
        "Switch",
        "Casse-briques",
        "Interrupteur"
      ]
    },
    "en": {
      "tagline": "A brick breaker where you don't catch the ball directly. Aim carefully to get as many bounces as possible in a single shot. Then tap the screen to turn the switches on and trap the ball between the bricks.",
      "tags": [
        "Switch",
        "Breakout",
        "Switch button"
      ]
    }
  },
  "description": "Coloured glass and banks of switches over a lake of lava. The ball breaks every pane of glass and flies straight past the dark buttons — until you tap: then they light up and turn solid, and the ball bounces off them and can never break them. Tap while the ball is inside a pocket of glass and it is shut in with it, runs faster and eats the whole room; tap again to let it out, or the game opens an empty pocket for you. Thirty boards across five biomes, each with its own bonus bricks: row and column blasts, bombs and multiball, the big ball, the fireball that burns through the glass and the magnet that pulls it in — and each biome brings its own living glass too: warp panes that jump every three seconds, split panes that burst into new glass, a seed that grows glass around it and electric panes behind a shield that comes and goes. Each biome teaches it in six stages — one colour, then all five and what each pays, its power, its living glass, the mix and a finale — and the stars are the wall's, not the score's: three fifths of it, nine tenths, and three for a clear within the level's par of balls. The dotted sight solves five bounces ahead.",
